`digits` leaves arena memory behind on every pass of this loop, which cannot release it after each pass because the allocation on line 14 is stored into memory, where this analysis stops following it, and neither can `count` when it returns, so all of it lives as long as the caller's memory does. Keep what a pass allocates out of locals declared outside the loop and out of memory older than the pass, or bracket the loop body with `Arena.mark()` and `Arena.release(m)`
